# djotls

{ % View README in HTML:
 https://black-desk.github.io/djot-html-preview?url=https://github.com/black-desk/djotls/blob/master/README.dj
 % }

[![codecov](
https://codecov.io/gh/black-desk/djotls/graph/badge.svg?token=GF5SAU9WIC
)](https://codecov.io/gh/black-desk/djotls)

::: warning

{*This project is at a very early stage and is not ready for production
use.*}

:::

djotls is a [`Djot`](https://djot.net) toolkit written in Rust, with a
parser, formatter (`djotfmt`) and language server (`djotls`).

## Build

``` bash
cargo build --release
```

## Install

``` bash
cargo install --path .
```

## Usage

You can check the usage by running:

``` bash
cargo run -r -- --help
```

Or after installing:

``` bash
djotfmt --help
djotls --help
```

## Language server

The `djotls` executable provides formatting, navigation, references,
heading outlines, completion and diagnostics over stdio. See the
[language server guide](docs/lsp.dj) for setup and scope.

## Contributing

See the [contribution guide](CONTRIBUTING.dj) for test prerequisites,
documentation updates and release procedures. The [Djot syntax
reference](third_party/djot/doc/syntax.md) is included through the
upstream submodule.

